  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — that the outcomes are negligible in difference and the preference should be based on the higher probability of a favorable outcome — is not reflected in the individual’s reasoning. Instead, the individual justifies the choice by citing the higher payout (2500 vs. 2400 Euros) when probabilities were nearly equal. This contradicts the stated rule of the decision reason, which would have led to preferring Lottery B (34% vs. 33%). The individual’s justification does not follow the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The reasoning is based on a different criterion (higher payout), not on the probability of a favorable outcome. Thus, the individual did not use the decision reason as described.",
